syntax:
In C++, move constructor and move assignment operator are implicitly generated if:

- The class has no user-declared copy constructor, copy assignment, move constructor, or move assignment.
- All data members are movable (support move semantics).

Explicitly defaulting a move operation:

ClassName() = default;

Move constructor example:

ClassName(ClassName&&) = default;

Move assignment example:

ClassName& operator=(ClassName&&) = default;

code_example:
struct MyClass {
    std::vector<int> data;
    // No user-defined copy or move constructors
};

// Compiler synthesizes move constructor and move assignment
MyClass obj1;
MyClass obj2 = std::move(obj1);

// If a member has a deleted move constructor, the class's move constructor is also deleted
struct Member {
    Member(const Member&) = delete;
    Member& operator=(const Member&) = delete;
};
struct Container {
    Member m;
};
// Container's move constructor is implicitly deleted because Member's move is deleted
